    "answer": {
      "short": "The wider-interval rate gives $35\\text{ m}$ from $t=4$, $37\\text{ m}$ from $t=6$, or $41\\text{ m}$ by interpolating between $t=2$ and $t=7$. The narrower interval gives $36\\text{ m}$, which is expected to be more accurate because its rate uses readings closer to $t=5$.",
      "worked": "The average rate over $[2,7]$ is\n$$r=\\frac{63-8}{7-2}=11\\text{ m/s}.$$\nApplying this rate from the nearby known reading at $t=4$ gives\n$$d(5)\\approx24+11(5-4)=35\\text{ m}.$$\nApplying it backwards from $t=6$ gives\n$$d(5)\\approx48-11(6-5)=37\\text{ m}.$$\nInterpolating between the endpoints of $[2,7]$ is also valid. This gives\n$$d(5)\\approx8+11(5-2)=41\\text{ m},$$\nwhich is the same as $63-11(7-5)=41\\text{ m}$.\nFor the narrower interval,\n$$\\begin{align*}r&=\\frac{48-24}{6-4}=12\\text{ m/s},\\\\d(5)&\\approx24+12(5-4)=36\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$\nStarting at $t=6$ also gives $48-12(6-5)=36\\text{ m}$. The $36\\text{ m}$ estimate is expected to be more accurate because the narrower-interval rate uses readings closer to $t=5$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
